education|Learning process broader than attending school is retained. Access improvement is an aim, not a completed result; Vietnamese remote-village context and uncountable system use match.
insight|Understanding rather than only a fact is the boundary. Family park use example aligns, with into complement and optional countable observations explained; classification remains unresolved.
over|Spatial above, movement across and visiting adverb have separate ordinals and syntactic complements. Lamp, dog and lunch visit are distinct contexts; Vietnamese preserves invitation rather than completed visit.
shore|Land-water edge not the water itself. Boat location and walk to village translate faithfully; sea/lake scope remains broad without asserting a specific geography or canonical synonym identity.
wardrobe|Source definition supports furniture while source example supports clothing collection; both distinct noun boundaries are drafted without Oxford ordinals. Vietnamese and examples deliberately distinguish storage from owned clothes.
